WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.001
-The album's out.
-I know!

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.970
-Congratulations!
-It's crazy. [ Laughs ]

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.138
-"In The Meantime" is the name
of the album.

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:07.707
It's beautiful.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.743
I was telling you,
I love the unboxing intro,

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.512
and you told me that's you
playing the drums on that?

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.414
-It is, yeah.
Yeah, it's me playing the drums.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.849
My friend John Levine was like,
"You should play on this,"

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:18.584
and I was like, "OK."
So I did.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:19.718
So, I --
-It's fantastic.

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:20.719
I love it.
-My drumming debut.

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:22.154
-I was complimenting the drums.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:23.356
I go, "I like how it got
faster."

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.490
And you're like, "Oh, actually,
that's me."

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.059
-That's actually me.
-Yeah.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:27.460
-If The Roots ever need
an extra...

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.628
-Yeah, we can always get in
there.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:29.795
-[ Laughs ] Yeah, sure.

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:31.197
-Always.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.132
"Shapeshifter", you released --

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.434
it has an interesting story
behind that.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.202
Where did you record that?

00:00:37.202 --> 00:00:38.771
-So, I recorded
"Shapeshifter" --

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:41.807
well, for anyone who knows me
personally, or even not --

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:42.775
I mean, I say this in
every interview.

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:44.711
I love Amy Winehouse.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:48.982
And so I was in this producer --
he's a legend.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.117
I mean, not this producer --
he's Salaam Remi.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.152
He's legendary,
and I was in his house.

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:55.488
I had one day off in Miami to go
and work with him,

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.656
and I went to go to his house,

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.124
and he has, like,
a little home studio,

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.525
and he, like,
played it down, whatever.

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:01.393
And then when we go there,
he starts showing me

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:03.996
around his studio,
and I knew that he was

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.798
a collaborator of Amy's,

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:07.700
but I didn't know
that they had written, like,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.869
all the music in that house.
So he's showing me around.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.404
He was like, "So this is where
she wrote, like,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.172
'Back to Black', and, like,
this tree is where she wrote,

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.240
you know, 'Tears Dry'."

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.008
And I'm, like, trying to,
like, act normal.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.910
Like, "Yes, I'm up here.
I'm up here."

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.945
-Yeah, we got you.
-Wonderful, yeah. Yes.

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:21.480
-You were like, "What?!"
-I was freaking out.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.749
-Can I climb that tree
and be right back?

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:23.950
Yeah! [ Laughs ] Yeah,
literally.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.451
I took a photo beside it,
of course.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:26.786
-You had to.
-It was -- I'm like,

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:27.753
"This is the craziest thing."

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.088
I mean, not only do I love him,

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:30.556
which was, like, such
a huge deal to work with him,

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:32.725
but then knowing that
it was, like, in the environment

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.794
where they made
those phenomenal,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.063
you know, songs.
-That's pretty cool.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.397
It starts with nothing.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:39.999
It's a blank piece of paper.
-Yeah.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.235
-And ends up being a song
that we're all singing.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.369
We all know
all the words to.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.171
-It's crazy.
-It's just a bizarre thing.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.807
It's so --
Well, it's such a talent.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.075
Do you remember the first --

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.811
Do you remember the first time
you were at a show

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.814
and someone was singing
your words back to you?

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.817
-Yeah, actually. Funnily enough,
it was in New York.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:00.853
Yeah, I did a little show
at the Knitting Factory.

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:03.756
It was like 200 people,
maybe just under 200 people,

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.092
and it was, like,
my first sold out show

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.294
and I was, like, freaking out.
I'm like, "Wow."

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.363
Like, "I've made it.
All these people are, like,

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.332
here to see me, and I sang
"Here", my first song.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:14.867
And they were, like,
singing the words back,

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.069
and it was, like,
such a bizarre thing

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.604
that people left
whatever they were doing

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.707
in their day to, like,
see me play.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.475
And then also, like,
that they knew the words.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.443
It was, like, the craziest --
It was such a trip.

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:25.745
-That's so cool.
-Such a cool -- yeah.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.214
-And you know, you keep going up
and up and up.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.615
-Thank you.
-I also get to hear your voice

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:32.885
on the -- is the "Blade Runner",
the new show on Adult Swim?

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:35.021
-Yeah, yeah. "Black Lotus".
It's crazy.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:37.223
-Yes. That's going to be wild.
-Yeah, so awesome!

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.091
Yeah, super exciting

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:40.359
-Because you've done
soundtracks, but I mean,

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:42.361
to do the actual theme --
-Yeah, it's a lot of --

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:43.529
It's a lot of my voice.

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:44.797
I'm sorry. Anyone who doesn't
like me

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:48.167
is gonna have to like,
skip, skip. [ Laughs ]

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.969
-The tough thing is that we
actually all love your voice.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.103
-Oh, thank you.
-So yeah, so yeah.

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:52.805
-Thanks! [ Laughs ]

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.440
-You're also
actually in it as well.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.108
-Yes, I am. Yeah. So they --

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:57.877
I guess they might have seen
what I did with

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.146
"The Willoughbys", like, my
first, like, you know,

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:03.116
animated debut, and they asked
if I wanted to play a character.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:06.452
So she's, like, a jazz singer
robot woman.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.220
Very different from Jane in
"The Willoughbys".

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.822
Like, totally different things.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.457
But yeah, they asked
if I wanted to to play her,

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:14.160
and so I get to be on an episode
which is so cool, too.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.628
Yeah.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.530
Here's Alessia Cara
in the new show

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.999
"Blade Runner: Black Lotus".
Take a look at this.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:20.933
♪♪

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:23.069
-You didn't run.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:26.405
-Replicants don't live
very long,

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:30.242
and sometimes I get impatient
to see what happens next.

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:32.778
♪♪

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:34.246
-If life's so short,

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:38.718
why spend it singing about
emotions you can't understand?

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.486
-What better use for a life
than to explore

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.221
the essential mysteries?

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:44.757
♪♪

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.327
Isn't that why you do
what you do?

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.594
-Yes!

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:49.595
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:51.263
Alessia Cara, everybody!

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:54.400
"Blade Runner: Black Lotus" will
be on Adult Swim

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.969
later this fall,
and Alessia's album,

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:59.439
"In The Meantime",
is out now.

